      friendship: 0
  - title: The library or the lab
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I've got an idea. A seed library. In the store, in the corner by the rack. Free.
    - You borrow seeds, grow them, and bring some back at the end of the season. Everybody's seeds, from everybody's gardens. Halmeoni's pumpkin first.
    - Or I take the internship. Learn exactly how AgriSeed does it, from the inside. Find something we can use against them. I'd be in that building every day.
    - You helped grow the pumpkins. You choose with me.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Start the seed library
      replyA:
      - The library! I'm going to need tiny envelopes. So many tiny envelopes.
      - And a sign. Lena will draw it. And Bea will help. Bea will definitely help.
      flagsA:
      - seed_library_planned
      optionB: Take the internship
      replyB:
      - The internship. Okay. I'll be careful.
      - I'll write everything down. Every test, every number. If they're hiding something, I'll find it.
      flagsB:
      - sooah_internship
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Borrowed seeds
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - Forty envelopes borrowed in the first week! Ada took the sweet peas. Mateo took a tree I've never heard of. Nia took 'whatever bugs like'.
    - And Bea brought back seeds from her university garden that nobody's grown here for fifty years.
    - 'At the end of the season, they''ll all come back. More than went out. That''s the thing about seeds: they come back with interest.'
    happy: 1
    ask:
